# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opel_Corsa
# Vauxhall Corsa B: the first UK Corsa after the Nova name was dropped.
# UK launch 14 April 1993; production 1993-2000. UK registrations rose from
# 51,608 (1993) to 86,779 (1999), consistently in the UK top ten.
#
# Colours: Estate Blue, Star Silver, Flame Red, Green. DVSA 1993-2000 shares:
# blue 23-25%, silver 9-25% rising, red 15-23%; green sits in the 20-25%
# "other" group and is retained as the signature 1990s colour. These four are
# the era-adjusted top set; black was the next measured colour at 8-9%.
# Paint names are Vauxhall marketing names for the approximate shades; the
# render values are approximations, not paint codes.
#
# Dates are staggered per colour by observed road presence. Weights total 50,
# about half the Escort Mk4's 100, matching the sales ratio.

